docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:43:| **2. C* crossing was stated too precisely** | **Resolved, with a small abstract ambiguity** | P.15: “With the frozen searches the pooled C∗ minus R3 difference changes sign between p = 0.01 and 0.02; with the doubled searches it is already −0.004 at 0.01.” The comparison is explicitly unresolved at both low rates. | Accurate for the main correction. The abstract’s clause about one market setting the frozen sign should explicitly refer to 0.02. |
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:44:| **3. “Survives moderate churn” concealed pooling** | **Resolved** | Abstract, p.1: “the pooled B3 minus R3 gap stays positive through 0.03, though negative on three markets there, and is negative at 0.05.” | Accurate. The vague word “moderate” is gone. |
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:45:| **4. Diagnostics were frozen-only and their timing unclear** | **Partly resolved** | Table 8, p.18, supplies both versions. Its caption says: “These statistics were defined after the results at p = 0.01 and 0.05 and before the runs at 0.02 and 0.03.” | Accurate about the completed changes. The zero-churn allocation row remains absent, and the split between replacing and non-replacing attacks is supplied in the text only at 0.05. |
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:47:| **6. The abstract printed −0.052 alone** | **Resolved** | Abstract, p.1, and conclusion, p.19: “B3 minus R3 is −0.052 (−0.033 with the doubled searches; the frozen value includes one failed search).” | Accurate. Replace “failed search” with the formal term “search-flagged cell”; see below. |
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:48:| **7. Conclusion claimed a result about the comparator class** | **Resolved** | P.19: “Against C∗, the one verified-history comparator run under churn”. P.16 explicitly denies a class-wide robustness result. | Accurate. |
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:49:| **8. Mechanism discussion covered only attackers that stay old** | **Partly resolved** | P.15 now gives audit-rate ranges for attacks that replace and attacks that stay old, under both search versions. | Accurate about the added ranges. **Inaccurate** that the omitted newest-identity frequencies need another diagnostics pass. Those values already exist in the supplied records. |
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:50:| **9. Churn search flags remained** | **Resolved as a disclosure request** | Abstract, p.1: “21 of the 72 churn doubling checks are flagged incomplete.” | Accurate that no churn cells were re-searched. Round 5 allowed disclosure as an alternative. The underlying search uncertainty remains. |
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:51:| **10. Package lacked the amendment and run drivers** | **Resolved for the named omissions** | `churn-plan-amendment-1.md` and the Run A/B drivers are present. This is a package correction, so there is no revised paper sentence. | Accurate. Full simulation reproduction remains outside this package’s scope. |
