docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:240:All supplied continuation records pass their stated incremental-improvement check within the permitted rounds. This establishes that check, **not global convergence or a bound on remaining search error**. No churn cells were included. The original registered decisions remain unchanged.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:250:That subtitle is honest. It resolves the previous ambiguity about whether the churn result was registered.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:252:The main structural problem is visible in the PDF: honest churn starts on p.14, its main table appears on p.16, its figure appears on p.17 after Section 11 has begun, and its audit-allocation table appears on p.18. The conclusion and Availability continue on p.19. The response’s statement that the main text ends on p.18 is incorrect.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:256:1. **Move the churn figure and its main empirical statement into the introduction.** Keep the full analysis in Section 10.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:259:4. **Split the long Q1 discussion.** Separate the registered result, search sensitivity and comparator-selection sensitivity.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:261:6. **Shorten the repeated FlashProve discussion.** It motivates costly checks, but does not carry the experimental contribution.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:262:7. **Keep the churn tables inside the churn section.**
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:264:The novelty should be stated narrowly. Credibility-based checking with identity replacement already appears in Sarmenta’s work, and BOINC’s adaptive replication uses verified history to vary checking. The paper acknowledges this correctly. Its contribution is the controlled comparison and the observed failure under honest turnover, rather than the basic idea of checking newcomers. [groups.csail.mit.edu](https://groups.csail.mit.edu/cag/bayanihan/papers/ccgrid01/ccgrid01.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:272:> “Reselecting each rule’s reference from its frozen menu under churn changes the reference in 32 of the 72 cells, by at most 0.009 in gain.” (p.15).
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:274:The reported maximum is a **training-score change**, not a measured bound on held-out gain. It is also approximately 0.009485, so “at most 0.009” is not a literal upper bound. Sources: P `flags.max_reference_change`; `churn_v2.py::reference_of`; `churn-plan.md`, §3.
