docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:296:> “These conclusions concern frozen searches and references, with interval calibration admitted on development fixtures.” (p.19).
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:298:The preceding conclusions include churn and reset results. Their percentile intervals are not the calibrated registered Q1/Q4 procedure. The paragraph also discusses doubled-search sensitivities.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:302:> “The registered Q1/Q4 inferences use calibration admitted on development fixtures. The follow-up intervals are exploratory and condition on the six markets, selected policies and frozen reference menus. Doubled searches are sensitivity analyses.”
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:308:The problematic sentence is quoted in Section 4(c). At one low rate the sign differs between search versions; at the other, one market determines the frozen pooled sign.
